WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.426
Hello, I'm Carl and I live in Lapu-Lapu City

00:00:02.276 --> 00:00:05.633
and my story involves waking up early on Saturdays

00:00:05.483 --> 00:00:07.978
to take cold showers before water is cut off.

00:00:08.121 --> 00:00:11.029
You see here power and water cuts are announced

00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:14.150
late on different pages often as images you

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.771
scroll through on Facebook and families find

00:00:16.621 --> 00:00:18.874
out too late to prepare which is why I built

00:00:18.724 --> 00:00:19.236
Abiso.

00:00:19.339 --> 00:00:22.368
In my interviews, we have a student that revises

00:00:22.218 --> 00:00:24.593
until 1 in the morning, only to find out that

00:00:24.443 --> 00:00:26.799
classes were suspended at 10.40 at night.

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:29.075
On a page, the family doesn't follow.

00:00:29.184 --> 00:00:31.799
Again, another mother says, Ligo na mo karon,

00:00:31.805 --> 00:00:33.851
or take a bath now, because the water cut

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:35.127
was announced the night before.

00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:37.696
So the drum gets filled, and everybody showers

00:00:37.546 --> 00:00:38.230
early.

00:00:38.339 --> 00:00:40.661
This family lost power and the pump in one

00:00:40.511 --> 00:00:43.558
night, so spoiled food, no shower, and a late

00:00:43.408 --> 00:00:46.455
start at work with a hot afternoon and nothing

00:00:46.305 --> 00:00:46.799
prepared.

00:00:47.115 --> 00:00:49.937
Unfortunately, this is expected in our day-to-day.

00:00:50.046 --> 00:00:52.558
The Power Company again posts brownouts as

00:00:52.408 --> 00:00:54.851
images you scroll past through, Water District

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:57.230
posts on its own site that barely loads, school

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:00.058
notices as PDFs, and don't mention the fourth

00:00:59.908 --> 00:01:01.161
Weather Bureau format.

00:01:01.305 --> 00:01:02.524
So many formats.

00:01:02.839 --> 00:01:03.937
Two things making this worse.

00:01:04.046 --> 00:01:06.093
Number one, since the Department of Education's

00:01:05.943 --> 00:01:09.058
Order 22 of 2024, brownout and heat suspensions

00:01:08.908 --> 00:01:11.317
are the mayor's call, making the post come

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:11.713
late.

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:14.299
Second, power and water, they're coupled,

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:17.541
so when the grid drops, 147 water pumps stop

00:01:17.391 --> 00:01:17.903
as well.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.834
with about one to two hours of warning.

00:01:20.149 --> 00:01:22.541
This is why Abiso reads every official notice

00:01:22.391 --> 00:01:24.075
once and turns it into an event.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.748
This here is the live prototype on Cloud Run,

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:30.161
recording 341 disruption events from 204 official

00:01:30.011 --> 00:01:30.610
posts.

00:01:30.632 --> 00:01:32.351
This is refreshed every 3 hours.

00:01:32.494 --> 00:01:36.024
For instance, today, in Basak, an MCWD water

00:01:35.874 --> 00:01:38.282
interruption for a mainline leak repair has

00:01:38.132 --> 00:01:40.610
been noticed, with the link of where it came

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:40.817
from.

00:01:41.132 --> 00:01:43.834
The good part is it uses natural language

00:01:43.684 --> 00:01:46.265
so they can just ask, Naay water interruptions

00:01:46.115 --> 00:01:46.920
sa Basak today?

00:01:47.132 --> 00:01:49.368
The question goes to a Gemini agent built

00:01:49.218 --> 00:01:51.541
with Google's agent development kit which

00:01:51.391 --> 00:01:53.679
then hands it to a water specialist that can

00:01:53.529 --> 00:01:54.989
only read the stored notices.

00:01:55.098 --> 00:01:58.058
The answer comes back in Cebuano with the

00:01:57.908 --> 00:01:59.817
water office's link.

00:02:00.132 --> 00:02:02.024
To prove it doesn't hallucinate, here's the

00:02:01.874 --> 00:02:02.679
developer UI.

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:05.334
See the tool call its results, reply, the

00:02:05.184 --> 00:02:07.041
trace from coordinator to the water agent,

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.110
and then back to the tool.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.661
No step answers from memory.

00:02:10.491 --> 00:02:12.124
But we don't want yet another webpage.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:14.435
That's why Abiso's real value is found in

00:02:14.285 --> 00:02:16.366
the family group chat where you already live.

00:02:16.474 --> 00:02:18.693
Here, Jen asks if there's a water interruption

00:02:18.543 --> 00:02:18.952
today.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.969
Mom tags Abiso and the reply is a live answer

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:23.676
from the same agent with proof.

00:02:23.785 --> 00:02:25.228
Now dad says, okay, let's fill the drum.

00:02:25.354 --> 00:02:25.710
Stat!

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:28.952
Then Migs forwards a poster from social media,

00:02:29.009 --> 00:02:31.676
then Abiso reads the image just for verification

00:02:31.526 --> 00:02:33.693
and then answers with the event it compiled.

00:02:33.543 --> 00:02:36.107
So the webhook really is built and public

00:02:35.957 --> 00:02:38.038
access awaits Meta's app review.

00:02:38.354 --> 00:02:39.572
Here's another example.

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:41.659
Are there classes tomorrow in Lapu-Lapu City?

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.676
Abiso doesn't find an official notice, so

00:02:43.526 --> 00:02:44.917
Abiso says exactly that.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.072
No hallucination.

00:02:46.388 --> 00:02:48.745
Under the hood, Cloud Scheduler wakes the

00:02:48.595 --> 00:02:50.952
Cloud Run every three hours, where Gemini

00:02:50.802 --> 00:02:53.745
3.8 flash on Vertex AI compiling each new

00:02:53.595 --> 00:02:55.159
post into a typed event.

00:02:55.354 --> 00:02:57.986
Type, barangay or the area affected, start,

00:02:58.164 --> 00:02:59.297
and status and source.

00:02:59.491 --> 00:03:02.072
A reconciler merges extensions and cancellations,

00:03:02.078 --> 00:03:05.072
and the events are stored in Firestore, with

00:03:04.922 --> 00:03:06.331
four doors reading one store.

00:03:06.422 --> 00:03:09.055
The webpage, the ask box agent, and a calendar

00:03:08.905 --> 00:03:11.245
per barangay, as well as the Messenger webhook.

00:03:11.095 --> 00:03:13.935
Other AI assistants can call it through MCP

00:03:13.785 --> 00:03:14.641
and A2A.

00:03:14.802 --> 00:03:17.521
One model call per notice, so questions cost

00:03:17.371 --> 00:03:17.883
nothing.

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.176
Benchmark time.

00:03:19.405 --> 00:03:23.004
I hand-labeled 50 posts to see if the AI models

00:03:22.854 --> 00:03:25.745
could categorize it the same way I, a human

00:03:25.595 --> 00:03:26.814
living in Lapu-Lapu, would.

00:03:26.922 --> 00:03:29.262
Thankfully, Gemini got the type right every

00:03:29.112 --> 00:03:29.659
single time.

00:03:29.974 --> 00:03:30.986
But does it work?

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:33.400
I sat down with five families who now use

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.366
Abiso because one of their stories was how

00:03:35.216 --> 00:03:38.176
this father would start his day going through

00:03:38.026 --> 00:03:39.917
Facebook and scrolling through all the notices

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:42.641
because the last time he missed one, all of

00:03:42.491 --> 00:03:43.900
the freezer food rotted.

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:46.417
In fact, this has caught the attention of

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:48.952
the mayor of the city who wants a demo, which

00:03:48.802 --> 00:03:51.141
I will attend to and hopefully get a memorandum

00:03:50.991 --> 00:03:52.193
of understanding from it.

00:03:52.273 --> 00:03:53.423
And that's Abiso.

00:03:53.635 --> 00:03:56.095
Official notices for Lapu-Lapu City compiled

00:03:55.945 --> 00:03:58.302
once and answered where people already are.

